# Crash-cause scan

`android-gotchas.mdc` is the **writing-time** rule (how to avoid bugs as you type). This rule is the **review-time** rule: before reporting a slice as done, scan the diff for the crash signatures below. If you find any, flag them in the response and either fix or call them out explicitly — do not silently ship.

## How to use this rule

When you have written or edited Kotlin / Compose / Gradle code in a slice, before saying "done":

1. Walk the **scan checklist** below against the files you touched (and any files you read that looked risky in passing).
2. For each hit, decide: **fix now** (in-scope) or **flag for follow-up** (out-of-scope but the user must know).
3. Cite hits inline using `path:line` so the user can jump straight there.

Pasabayan repo grep idioms (use these to scan):

```bash
# Null-assertion & cast crashes (§1)
grep -rn --include="*.kt" -E '!!|\bas [A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_<>?]+($|[^?])' app/src/main core/*/src/main

# lateinit usage (§1)
grep -rn --include="*.kt" "lateinit var" app/src/main core/*/src/main

# GlobalScope / wrong scope (§2, §5)
grep -rn --include="*.kt" -E "GlobalScope|runBlocking\(" app/src/main core/*/src/main

# Main-thread I/O risk (§4)
grep -rn --include="*.kt" -E "\.execute\(\)|HttpURLConnection|Thread\.sleep" app/src/main core/*/src/main

# Hardcoded colors / hex — separate rule, but a frequent style/crash overlap in dark mode (§6)
grep -rn --include="*.kt" -E 'Color\(0x[0-9A-Fa-f]{8}\)|Color\.(White|Black)' app/src/main
```

(Adjust the path scope to what your slice touched; don't grep the world.)

